  "question_text": "<p>How do you draw the lumped-element electrical model for a lossless transmission line?</p>",
  "answer_text": "<img src=\"{{image_1}}\" alt=\"A schematic labeled 'Transmission Line' showing a cascaded LC ladder network. It consists of multiple series inductors (L1, L2, L3...) and multiple shunt capacitors (C1, C2, C3...) connecting the nodes between the inductors to ground.\" style=\"max-width:100%;margin:1rem 0;border-radius:6px;\"/>\n<p>It is drawn as a ladder of series inductors (L) and shunt capacitors (C) connected to ground.</p>",
  "explanation_text": "<p>Even a straight piece of wire has parasitic effects. The wire itself acts as a small inductor (L), and its physical separation from the ground plane underneath it acts as a small capacitor (C).</p>",
